box policy is applied to a user’s mailbox, all the managed folders that are linked to the policy are deployed in a single operation, thereby making the deployment of messaging records management (MRM) easier.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2161198">UM mailbox policy</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ga-IE"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2297589">polasaí bosca ríomhphoist i gcomhair fillteán bainistithe</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">IRL</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Masculine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="15_397203_2297589"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A logical grouping of managed folders. When a managed folder mailbox policy is applied to a user’s mailbox, all the managed folders that are linked to the policy are deployed in a single operation, thereby making the deployment of messaging records management (MRM) easier.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="397203">managed folder mailbox policy</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ga-IE"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2297589">polasaí bosca ríomhphoist i gcomhair fillteán bainistithe</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">IRL</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Masculine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="1500_7883_512598"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">Pertaining to an entity such as the device, program, file, record or portion of the screen that is currently operational or subject to command operations.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="7883">active</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Adjective</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ga-IE"><ntig><termGrp><term id="512598">gníomhach</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">IRL</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Adjective</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="15015_184144_513688"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The title for a dialog that specifies how a signature line should be signed, including instructions for signers.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="184144">Signature Setup</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ga-IE"><ntig><termGrp><term id="513688">Cumraíocht Sínithe</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">IRL</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Feminine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="15022_319430_514332"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">Having a frequency in the electromagnetic spectrum in the range just below that of red light.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="319430">infrared</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Adjective</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ga-IE"><ntig><termGrp><term id="514332">infridhearg</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">IRL</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Adjective</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><ter