hical user interface), with another program such as the operating system, or with the computer's hardware.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="68580">interface</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ga-IE"><ntig><termGrp><term id="513038">comhéadan</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">IRL</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Masculine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="1883_318780_514308"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The = character.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="318780">equal sign</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ga-IE"><ntig><termGrp><term id="514308">comhartha 'cothrom le'</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">IRL</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Masculine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="18831_651182_1818352"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A character that does not have strong right-to-left or left-to-right language attributes.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="651182">neutral character</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ga-IE"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1818352">carachtar neodrach</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">IRL</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Masculine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="18840_651191_1818353"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A file you create on your hard disk or a network share to store OLAP source data for a PivotTable or PivotChart report. Offline cube files allow you to keep working when you are not connected to the OLAP server.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="651191">offline cube file</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ga-IE"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1818353">comhad ciúib as líne</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">IRL</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Masculine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="1885_69963_1260778"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The ability for two or more software applications to work together with little effort from the user.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="69963">interoperability</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Mass</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ga-IE"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1260778">comh-inoibritheacht</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">IRL</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="18851_651202_1468340"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The result of assigning more tasks to a resource than the resource can accomplish in the working time available.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="651202">overallocation</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ga-IE"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1468340">ró-leithdháileadh</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">IRL</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="18860_651211_1792282"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">Principles that guide developers as they assign responsibilities to software classes and design system behavior. They are most useful when creating collaboration diagrams where messages imply responsibility.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="651211">patterns</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Plural</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ga-IE"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1792282">patrúin</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">IRL</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Plural</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="18862_651213_1818354"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A field that you use to enter or display how much of a task has been completed. This value is expressed as the percentage of the task duration that has been completed.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="651213">percent complete</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ga-IE"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1818354">céatadán críochnaithe</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">IRL</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Masculine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="18865_651216_1095514"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A view of a list, SharePoint document library, or Web Part Page that is available only to a particular user.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="651216">personal view</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ga-IE"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1095514">amharc pearsanta</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">IRL</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Masculine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="18866_651217_1522704"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A shared Web Part that has been modified by a user in personal view. The changes made to a Web Part personalized in this way are visible only to the user who made those changes.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="651217">personalized Web Part</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ga-IE"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1522704">Comhpháirt Gréasáin phearsanta</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">IRL</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Masculine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="18873_651224_1468341"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A schedule of task start and finish dates and resource and cost data.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="651224">plan</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ga-IE"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1468341">plean</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">IRL</termN