icalUsage">IRL</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="38879_2259611_2434524"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">To add a shortcut to an application or part of an application or contact by fixing its tile to the Start screen (the full screen view of Start) or Start menu.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2259611">pin to Start</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Verb</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ga-IE"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2434524">pionnáil le 'Tosaigh'</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">IRL</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Verb</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="3888_25223_512705"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A communication line used for data transfer among the components of a computer system.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="25223">bus</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ga-IE"><ntig><termGrp><term id="512705">bus</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">IRL</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Masculine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="38880_2259632_2260974"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">In the Windows Store for Business and Education Store, to get apps and other digital goods into the hands of employees or students.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2259632">distribute</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Verb</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ga-IE"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2260974">dáileadh</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">IRL</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Verb</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="38882_2259634_2260976"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A feature that lets customers extend their gaming experience across multiple devices, play with other users, and show off scores and achievements.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2259634">game hub</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ga-IE"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2260976">lárionad cluichí</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">IRL</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="38883_2259635_2260978"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The default browser in Windows 10, which provides a more interoperable, reliable, and discoverable experience with advanced features including the ability to annotate on web pages, a distraction-free reading experience, and integration of Cortana. Also available on iOS and Android.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2259635">Microsoft Edge</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ga-IE"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2260978">Microsoft Edge</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">IRL</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="38884_2259636_2261291"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The source location of files that are stored on OneDrive and not synced to the local device. This is different from other OneDrive files (just called "OneDrive"), where a copy is synced and stored locally as well as in the cloud.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2259636">OneDrive (cloud only)</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ga-IE"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2261291">OneDrive (sa néal amháin)</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">IRL</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="38885_2259637_2261300"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A user role within Windows Store for Business that allows the user to acquire apps from Windows Store for Business on behalf of his company.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2259637">purchaser</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ga-IE"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2261300">ceannaitheoir</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">IRL</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="38886_2259638_2261307"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A view of a set of photos that displays them one at a time, sequentially.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2259638">slideshow</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ga-IE"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2261307">taispeántas sleamhnán</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">IRL</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="38887_2259809_2261288"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The section in the Settings app for Windows 10 desktop, containing network and Internet settings.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2259809">Network &amp; Internet</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ga-IE"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2261288">Líonra &amp; Idirlíon</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">IRL</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="38892_2897506_2897670"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The Microsoft cloud-based filtering system that detects and blocks malicious files, attachments, malware, and links in team sites, document libraries, as well as in team collaboration and email apps.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2897506">Microsoft Defender for Office 365</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ga-IE"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2897670">Microsoft Defender le haghaidh Office 365</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">IRL</termNote><