ecurity product experience for protecting Windows devices and users from malware and other threats.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="3073145">Defender</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ga-IE"><ntig><termGrp><term id="3075112">Microsoft Defender</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">IRL</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="43467_3073145_3075196"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The Microsoft Security product experience for protecting Windows devices and users from malware and other threats.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="3073145">Defender</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ga-IE"><ntig><termGrp><term id="3075196">Defender</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">IRL</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="43468_2721513_2722178"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The feature that helps to isolate enterprise-defined untrusted sites based on a list of trusted web sites, cloud resources and internal networks defined by an enterprise administrator. Everything not on that list is considered untrusted.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2721513">Application Guard</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ga-IE"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2722178">Cosaint Feidhmchláir</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">IRL</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="43468_2721513_3085729"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The feature that helps to isolate enterprise-defined untrusted sites based on a list of trusted web sites, cloud resources and internal networks defined by an enterprise administrator. Everything not on that list is considered untrusted.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2721513">Application Guard</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ga-IE"><ntig><termGrp><term id="3085729">Cosaint Feidhmchláir Microsoft Defender</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">IRL</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Feminine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="43468_2795831_2722178"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The feature that helps to isolate enterprise-defined untrusted sites based on a list of trusted web sites, cloud resources and internal networks defined by an enterprise administrator. Everything not on that list is considered untrusted.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2795831">Microsoft Defender Application Guard</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ga-IE"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2722178">Cosaint Feidhmchláir</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">IRL</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="43468_2795831_3085729"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The feature that helps to isolate enterprise-defined untrusted sites based on a list of trusted web sites, cloud resources and internal networks defined by an enterprise administrator. Everything not on that list is considered untrusted.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2795831">Microsoft Defender Application Guard</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ga-IE"><ntig><termGrp><term id="3085729">Cosaint Feidhmchláir Microsoft Defender</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">IRL</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Feminine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="43471_2795848_3085731"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The name of a Windows feature that enables IT to lock down devices so they can only use trusted devices and peripherals, and provides the capability to isolate parts of the operating system by using virtualization-based security (VBS).​</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2795848">Microsoft Defender Device Control</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ga-IE"><ntig><termGrp><term id="3085731">Rialú Gléasanna Microsoft Defender</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">IRL</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Masculine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="43472_2795843_3085733"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The umbrella name for the Windows vulnerability mitigation features designed to address inherently technical attacks and prevent discovered vulnerabilities from being exploited.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2795843">Microsoft Defender Exploit Guard</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ga-IE"><ntig><termGrp><term id="3085733">Cosaint Ar Theacht Aniar Microsoft Defender</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">IRL</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Feminine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="4349_58489_512977"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">Pertaining to an entire entity such as document, file, or program rather than to a restricted segment of it.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="58489">global</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Adjective</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ga-IE"><ntig><termGrp><term id="512977">uilíoch</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">IRL</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Adjective</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="43506_2462246_2465995"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The mixed-reality shell experience, in which content can be placed and used in virtual (or, in the case of HoloLens, real) surroundings.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2462246">mixed world</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ga