usiness such as to fill service requests, place orders, or connect to another respondent or another call.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2841643">call agent</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ga-IE"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2842275">gníomhaire</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">IRL</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="50216_2841643_2842279"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A person who handles a call to a business such as to fill service requests, place orders, or connect to another respondent or another call.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2841643">call agent</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ga-IE"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2842279">gníomhaire glaonna</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">IRL</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="50216_2841644_2842275"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A person who handles a call to a business such as to fill service requests, place orders, or connect to another respondent or another call.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2841644">agent</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ga-IE"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2842275">gníomhaire</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">IRL</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="50216_2841644_2842279"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A person who handles a call to a business such as to fill service requests, place orders, or connect to another respondent or another call.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2841644">agent</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ga-IE"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2842279">gníomhaire glaonna</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">IRL</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="50217_2841650_2842281"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">In a call queue, a method of sending calls to agents whereby routing of incoming calls is balanced so that each call agent gets the same number of calls from the queue.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2841650">round robin</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ga-IE"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2842281">timdháileadh comh-agach</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">IRL</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="50219_2841716_2842280"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A feature of the Microsoft Teams Admin Center that shows detailed information about the devices, networks, and connectivity related to the calls and meetings for each user in a Microsoft Teams or Skype for Business tenant account. It is displayed on the user's Call History tab.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2841716">Call Analytics</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ga-IE"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2842280">Anailísíocht glaonna</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">IRL</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="50220_2841736_2842276"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">Information that gives insight into usage patterns and activity.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2841736">analytics</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ga-IE"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2842276">Anailísíocht</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">IRL</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="50221_2841755_2842277"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">In Microsoft teams, name of a tab on the Manage teams dialog that displays team analytics.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2841755">Analytics</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ga-IE"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2842277">anailísíocht</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">IRL</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="50222_2841766_2842278"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">In a call queue, a method of sending calls to agents whereby the first call in the queue rings all call agents at the same time. The first call agent to pick up the call gets the call.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2841766">attendant routing</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Other</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ga-IE"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2842278">ródú cúntóra</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">IRL</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Other</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="50235_2842094_2845128"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">During an active meeting, to invite more people to join the meeting by dialing their phone number.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2842094">dial out</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Verb</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ga-IE"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2845128">diailigh amach</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">IRL</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Verb</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="50235_2842094_2845130"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">During an active meeting, to invite more people to join the meeting by dialing their phone number.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2842094">dial out</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Verb</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">