 of a given set of integers.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2956715">greatest common factor</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ga-IE"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2957251">comhfhachtóir is mó</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">IRL</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Masculine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="52736_2956716_2957314"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">Of a number or expression, a number which, when raised to a specified power, yields the specified number or expression.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2956716">root</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ga-IE"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2957314">fréamh</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">IRL</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Feminine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="52737_2956717_2957323"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">An expression consisting of three terms.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2956717">trinomial</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ga-IE"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2957323">slonn tríthéarmach</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">IRL</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Masculine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="52738_2956718_2957294"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A polynomial equation of the second degree.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2956718">quadratic equation</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ga-IE"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2957294">cothromóid chearnach</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">IRL</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Feminine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="52739_2956719_2957272"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A multiplicative factor consisting of a whole number.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2956719">Integer coefficient</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ga-IE"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2957272">comhéifeacht slánuimhreach</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">IRL</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Feminine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="5274_168784_513642"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">To go back to a previous state by reversing the effects of one or more commands.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="168784">undo</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Verb</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ga-IE"><ntig><termGrp><term id="513642">cealaigh</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">IRL</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Verb</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</ter