pages, and the number of bits that can be used by the kernel to address physical memory can be expanded from 32 to 36.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="92107">PAE</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ga-IE"><ntig><termGrp><term id="513214">breisiú seoltaí fisiciúla</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">IRL</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Masculine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="5870_92107_513215"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A feature that allows x86-based computers to support more than 4 gigabytes (GB) of physical memory. Up to 64 GB of physical memory can be used as regular 4-kilobyte (KB) pages, and the number of bits that can be used by the kernel to address physical memory can be expanded from 32 to 36.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="92107">PAE</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ga-IE"><ntig><termGrp><term id="513215">PAE</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">IRL</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="5874_101275_1818059"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A form of statistical analysis used for forecasting. Regression analysis estimates the relationship between variables so that a given variable can be predicted from one or more other variables.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="101275">regression analysis</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelec