that is contained in a digital media file or stream.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="152809">content</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Mass</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ga-IE"><ntig><termGrp><term id="513589">inneachar</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">IRL</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Masculine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Mass</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="9091_358353_2297429"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A set of components and services that enable users to access their Exchange mailboxes through the application Outlook Web Access and the protocols Exchange ActiveSync, Post Office Protocol version 3 (POP3), and Internet Message Access Protocol 4rev1 (IMAP4). The Client Access server role also includes Web services that are used by other Exchange 2007 server roles.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="358353">Client Access server role</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ga-IE"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2297429">ról freastalaí rochtana ar an gcliant</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">IRL</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Masculine</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="910_748601_1260766"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A collection of email addresses that is treated as a single recipient for email distribution purposes, and that is created by and available to an individual Outlook user.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="748601">contact group</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammatic